.TH cghex 1 "November 2026" "cgtools 1.4.0"
.\" one space after a full stop, not the sentence space roff adds
.ss 12 0
.SH NAME
cghex \- a binary file editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cghex
.RI [ "toolkit options" ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B CGHex
shows the bytes of any file and lets them be changed, either as
hexadecimal or as text: the hexadecimal digits are on the left, the
same bytes as ASCII on the right, and the offset of each line before
them. Clicking in either side puts the cursor there, and what is typed
goes into that side: the digits 0 to 9 and a to f on the left, any
printable character on the right.
.PP
Each file given opens on a page of its own in the one window, and the
.B Files
menu lists every open file.
.B View \(-> Add view
opens a second view of the same file, on a page of its own; a change
made in one view shows in all.
.PP
.B Edit \(-> Insert mode
(or the Insert key) chooses between inserting bytes and writing over
them.
.B Edit \(-> Group Data As
shows the hexadecimal side in bytes, words of 16 bits or longwords of
32. Changes can be undone and redone, as many times as the preferences
allow.
.PP
.B Find
and
.B Replace
look for a string of hexadecimal digits or of ASCII text, forward or
backward.
.B Jump to Byte
moves the cursor to an offset, given in decimal or, after 0x, in
hexadecimal.
.PP
.B File \(-> Export to HTML
writes the file out as a set of web pages, one table of hexadecimal and
text to a page, with links between them.
.PP
.B Tools \(-> Converter
turns a number between binary, octal, decimal, hexadecimal and ASCII,
and can take the value at the cursor.
.B Tools \(-> Character Table
lists the 256 byte values in each of these; a double click on a row
puts that byte in at the cursor.
.PP
The preferences choose the font, how many changes can be undone, how
the cursor's offset is shown in the status bar (in decimal,
hexadecimal, or a printf format of your own with one %d, %o, %x or
%X), whether the offsets column is shown, and how new views group
their data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Take everything after it as a file, even when it starts with a dash.
.PP
The usual GTK options, such as
.BR \-\-display ,
are also understood.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cghex/cghexrc
The preferences.
Without the variable,
.I ~/.config/cghex/cghexrc
is used.
.SH AUTHORS
CGHex is GHex 1.2.1, made a plain CGTK program. GHex was written by
Jaka Mocnik, with Chema Celorio.
